   "OverallSummary": "This case involves Care Obligation violations by Alfred S. Vanderlaan who recommended speculative, unrated GWG L Bonds to two retail customers with moderate risk tolerances. The violations specifically fall under Rule 15l-1(a)(1) of Regulation Best Interest (Reg BI) and FINRA Rule 2010. The analytical steps to determine the Care Obligation violations were: 1) Review of customers' investment profiles including risk tolerance, investment objectives, and financial situations; 2) Assessment of the high-risk nature of the GWG L Bonds which were speculative, unrated, and illiquid; 3) Evaluation of the concentration risk created by the recommendations (over 20% of liquid net worth in alternative investments for both customers); and 4) Determination that recommendations were not in the customers' best interests based on their investment profiles. For Customer A (a senior investor), Vanderlaan recommended a $50,000 investment in GWG L Bonds despite the customer already having $135,000 in alternative investments, which increased alternative investment concentration beyond 20% of liquid net worth. For Customer B, Vanderlaan recommended two additional investments totaling $115,000 in GWG L Bonds, despite the customer already having $100,000 in L Bonds and $15,000 in other alternative investments, which resulted in over 21% of liquid net worth in L Bonds. Both customers had moderate risk tolerances and investment objectives of growth and income, not speculation. Vanderlaan earned $6,508 in commissions from these transactions. GWG L Bonds defaulted in January 2022 and GWG filed for bankruptcy in April 2022. As sanctions, Vanderlaan was suspended for three months, fined $10,000, and ordered to pay $6,508 in restitution plus interest to the affected customers."
